### Scientific Experience

**07.2023 – present**  
**Conformational Dynamics of Kinases**  
*Charité Universitätsmedizin Berlin (guest scientist at [Universität des Saarlandes](https://volkamerlab.org/))  
Prof. A. Volkamer, Einstein BIH Visiting Fellow John Chodera, PhD*  
- Conformational dynamics of inhibitor-bound kinases under mutagenesis conditions.  
- Pipeline for large-scale conformational analysis of the structural kinome.  
- Integration of kinase-specific generic residue numbering into [mdciao](https://mdciao.org)*  
- pH-dependent conformational switching


**07.2018 – present**  
**Molecular Simulation and Automated Analysis of GPCRs and GPCR–G protein Complexes**  
*Charité Universitätsmedizin Berlin (guest scientist at [Universität Leipzig](https://proteinformatics.uni-leipzig.de/group/team.php))  
Prof. P. W. Hildebrand, Dr. Patrick Scheerer, Einstein BIH Visiting Fellow Prof. Brian Kobilka*  
- Implementation of adaptive sampling protocols.  
- Group-wide support for simulation methodologies and infrastructure.  
- Automated MD analysis workflows and custom Python modules.  
- Development and release of open-source tool [mdciao](https://mdciao.org).

**01.2012 – 06.2018**  
**Markov Modeling, Adaptive Sampling, Software Development**  
*Freie Universität Berlin — Prof. F. Noé*  
- Molecular simulation of rhodopsin activation and conformational dynamics.  
- Development of dimensionality reduction techniques (e.g., TICA).  
- Refactoring of [PyEMMA's](http://emma-project.org/latest) API, especially the *coordinates* submodule.  
- Co-authorship and delivery of multiple PyEMMA tutorials to the community.

**12.2010 – 12.2011**  
**Molecular Simulation of Water in Carbon Nanotubes**  
*Freie Universität Berlin — PD Dr. B. Schmidt*  
- Confinement effects and transport phenomena of water inside carbon nanotubes.

**09.2005 – 11.2010**  
**Quantum Chemistry, Spectroscopy, and Laser Control of Molecular Rotors**  
*Friedrich-Schiller-Universität Jena — Prof. L. González*  
*Freie Universität Berlin — Prof. J. Manz, PD Dr. L. González*  
- Ground- and excited-state conformational dynamics and spectroscopy of light-triggered molecular rotors.  
- Quantum control approaches for laser-driven conformational transitions.


